The plan shows an intersection of Horizontal and Vertical streets (the side of each cell is 5 meters, and the crossings are shown as dotted lines). The traffic lights alternate with a period of 2 minutes according to the following schedule:

• 40 seconds -- green light for pedestrians crossing the Horizontal street;
• the next 20 seconds -- red for all pedestrians;
• the following 40 seconds -- green for those crossing the Vertical street;
• and the last 20 seconds -- red for all pedestrians.

Edgar walks at a speed of 1 m/s. At a random moment, he finds himself at point A, from where he crosses to point B in the fastest way possible, without breaking the rules. Edgar can see how much time is left until the change of signal at each traffic light, so he does not start crossing the street if he cannot finish in time. How many seconds on average will it take Edgar to reach point B?

